Z||000008||MinnGreenGT||12-26-2001||12:47 PM||||MSIE is "MicroSoft Internet Explorer"  and FTP is "File Transfer Protocol".  I know that you all understand MSIE now... no further explanation needed.  I'll try to make this a link <A HREF="ftp://24.20.244.178" TARGET=_blank>ftp://24.20.244.178</A> Anyway, put the "ftp://24.20.244.178" in your address bar like any other address.  If it asks you for a username & password, type in "pennock" for both.  If it doesn't ask for a password, select "connect as..." from the file menu.<P>An FTP client is a FTP specific control program.  Go to <A HREF="http://www.tucows.com" TARGET=_blank>http://www.tucows.com</A>  and check for a popular FTP client.  Similiar to a web browser, just works specifically on FTP (you put in a username, password, and address/directory).<P>------------------<BR>              <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/GreenGT6.gif"> ||||reg||1
